---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
import { href } from '../../lib/url'
---
<SiteLayout title="Blog" path="blog" description="Notes from building Nova, a self-hosted native language and IDE.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> Field notes</span>
      <h1>Build logs from the<br /><span style="color: var(--yellow)">compiler basement.</span></h1>
      <p>Short, evidence-first posts about the language, the Nova compiler and the workbench. No roadmap fiction.</p>
      <div class="hero-pill" style="margin-top: 22px;"><span>Self-hosting notes from the compiler basement</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="card blog-card">
        <div class="kicker">Launch note · November 2026</div>
        <h2><a href={href('blog/building-nova-in-rust/')}>Nova compiles itself now</a></h2>
        <p class="section-intro">How the compiler and language server became self-hosted, what a real native pipeline buys us, and the honest list of what Nova still cannot do.</p>
        <div class="meta">Self-hosting · LLVM · Nova Studio · 8 min read</div>
        <a class="button" href={href('blog/building-nova-in-rust/')}>Read the post <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
